We assign Drone_4, Drone_5, and Drone_8 to Field_1, covering 3 out of 4 drones needed. Thus, we need one more drone. The next closest is Drone_1.

Now, all 4 drones (Drone_4, Drone_5, Drone_8, and Drone_1) are assigned to Field_1 for protection. 

Now we need to distribute the remaining drones (Drone_2, Drone_3, Drone_6, and Drone_7) among the remaining fields. Since Field_4 and Field_2 have the next highest threat levels (both at 0.11), we will prioritize protecting them.

For Field_4, we require 3 total for full protection and currently have 0. We can only provide Drone_2 which is idle, and it will make a small contribution toward protection.

Next, we have Field_2 also needing 4 drones and currently having 0. This means Drone_3 will be assigned to Field_2. 

Field_3 is the least threatened and needs only 2 drones for full protection but currently has 0. We have no remaining drones to assign here, thus it will remain unprotected.

Finally, we have the following assignments:

